\f0\fs24 \cf0 Citation Verification Tool Build\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Context: I am building a citation-verification tool for the Life Sciences hackathon. Given a scientific claim and the paper cited for it, it checks whether the paper actually supports the claim, detects scope mismatch (species, population, model system), and checks retraction status. I want to understand exactly what you can do for the data and grounding parts of this build, so please be concrete about your capabilities and report what you actually used.\cb1 \
\cb3 Please do the following and show your work at each step:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
For a real PubMed record of your choosing, retrieve and report:\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
the abstract\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl1\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
the MeSH organism and population tags on the record (for example Humans, Animals, Mice, Rats, Adult, Child), pulled from the record metadata, not inferred from the text\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl1\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
the current retraction or expression-of-concern status\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cb3 For each item, tell me which database or connector you used.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
List the databases and connectors you can reach that are relevant to citation checking, specifically anything touching PubMed, MeSH, NCBI Taxonomy, and retraction data.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Take this sample: the claim "Compound X reduces tumor growth in humans" cited to a paper that studied only mice. Show me how your built-in citation fact-checker evaluates whether the citation supports the claim. Then tell me the mechanism: does your check grade the claim against structured record metadata and external ground-truth data, or does it re-evaluate using the same model reading the text?\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Tell me whether I can save a grounding routine as a reusable skill: one that takes a PMID and returns the abstract, the MeSH organism and population tags, and the retraction status in a structured format.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 End by summarizing, in plain terms, which parts of a citation-grounding pipeline you can handle natively and which parts I would need to build myself.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb4 I'll work through this concretely \'97 discovering what's actually available, then using it on a real record. Let me start by surveying the connectors and skills relevant to citation checking.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

