\fs36 \cf2 \cb4 Two selection findings that need a decision from you\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs30 \cf2 \cb4 Category A \'97 acknowledged vs uncritical citations. Many papers citing the Wakefield study explicitly call it "fraudulent" or "retracted." Ground truth ("cited paper is retracted") holds either way, but the more useful stress-test for your tool is an uncritical citation that treats the retracted finding as valid. Both types exist in the pool. My plan: prefer uncritical citing claims, and add a 
\fs28 \cf9 \cb10 citer_acknowledges_retraction
\fs30 \cf2 \cb4  field so you can filter. I'd also lean toward lower-profile retractions over Wakefield, since infamous cases get cited critically.\cb1 \
\cb4 Category B \'97 the mismatch lives in the claim's wording. The cited paper's animal-only scope is fully metadata-grounded (MeSH), but whether a citing claim over-generalizes to humans depends on how it's phrased. Citers that correctly say "in mice" are not mismatches. Only claims that drop the species qualifier or assert human/clinical relevance count. So Category B will carry more 
\fs28 \cf9 \cb10 model-inferred
\fs30 \cf2 \cb4  flags (on the claim-scope side) than A or C \'97 honestly marked and kept separate, per your rules.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb4 My recommendation: proceed as-is with those two adjustments baked in. A couple of options on scope if you'd like to steer:\cb1 \
\cb4 Pilot yield is ample. Do you want me to proceed to the full build, and how should I bias Category A (retracted) case selection?\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf6 \cb4 Proceed to the full build, all three categories. Category A selection: - Prefer uncritical citing claims that treat the retracted finding as still valid, over ones that acknowledge the retraction. The uncritical case is the real test of retraction detection. - Within that, the claim must actually rely on the specific retracted finding, not just cite the retracted paper in passing for an unrelated methodological point. Drop passing-mention citations even if uncritical. - Bias toward lower-profile retractions (which tend to be cited uncritically), but keep 1-2 recognizable ones for realism and demo legibility. - Every Category A row carries the citer_acknowledges_retraction flag in the final schema, so results can be sliced by hard (uncritical) vs easy (acknowledged). Keep B and C as planned. Run through to the assembled table and present it inline.\cf6 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

